## Context: the label is not the diagnosis

This review supersedes the subject-only merging recommendation in
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) and
[the old triage guide](/kb/triage/dedupe). The accepted decision record is preserved unchanged.
This replacement is **proposed**, not approval on behalf of the support desk.

The [incident page for #4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says “one issue, one fix queued.”
Its computed table contradicts that claim. A known label and a queued fix do not mean
every report has the same cause, or that either problem is fixed.

This is a review of the export dated 2026-10-04, not live access to the desk.
The reviewed date records this review; it does not make old exported data current.
Check later reports before making a current operational claim.

## What the reports cover

<IncidentReview />

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

### Parser: day-first dates read month-first

The shared parser interprets dates as MM/DD even when the tenant uses day-first dates.
For example, `harbour.dental` uses `en-GB` and `booking-v2`; `R-41200` describes
7 April becoming 4 July. The adjacent `R-41201` corrects that account in the other
direction. Their wording differs, but the tenant and input path identify the parser cause.

This group includes app and email reports, plus forms whose hint already agrees with
the tenant locale. Keep a parser ticket for this group. Fix the shared parser to respect
the tenant's date order, reject ambiguous input where appropriate, and test app, email,
and booking-v2 paths. Verify both ambiguous dates and dates with a day greater than twelve.

### Hint: booking-v3 tells people to use the wrong order

For day-first tenants using booking-v3, the form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` while interpreting
input using the tenant's day-first order. Following the displayed hint therefore produces
the wrong date. This is a separate UI/input contract bug, not a duplicate parser report.

Examples are `R-41230` (`copper.studio`, `es-ES`), `R-41241`
(`alder.physio`, `de-DE`), and `R-41251` (`pale.harbour`, `pt-PT`).
All came through the form. Use a separate ticket: make the displayed hint and parser agree
with the tenant locale; test all affected booking-v3 locales. A shared-parser fix alone
does not establish that this hint is correct.

### Keep uncertainty visible

Reports `R-41202`, `R-41209`, `R-41236`, `R-41344`, and `R-41620` have unusual
one-day or timing descriptions. The supplied cause logic and desk notes keep them under
the parser group by tenant and channel. Preserve their IDs and descriptions for follow-up;
do not invent a proven timezone cause from prose alone, and do not silently drop them.

## Decision proposed: merge only when the cause matches

1. Deduplicate export rows by report ID before counting; repeated rows are not new reports.
2. Look up the tenant's locale and booking form. Do not use browser locale or the intake tag as the diagnosis.
3. Apply `causeOf` from `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, using the report channel and tenant record.
4. Merge only reports with the same established cause. Equal subject lines are neither necessary nor sufficient.
5. Keep unknown tenants or unclassified reports separate for investigation. Missing evidence is not a merge rule.
6. Record report IDs and counts on each ticket; reclassify new reports as they arrive.

The executable examples below contrast different subjects with the same cause, equal
subjects with different causes, and unknown tenants. The displayed results run the same
classification logic as the count table.

<DedupeExplorer />

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not follow the old guide's “when unsure, merge” instruction. Keep unclassified reports
apart until the tenant and cause are known. Submit this replacement for desk review.
</Callout>

## What the timeline actually shows

The chart distinguishes receipt time from merge time. A batch merge is work on the queue,
not evidence that the underlying product suddenly broke on the merge date. Reports continue
after the batch and through the export cutoff; “known” is not “resolved.”

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

